---
description: Keep backend layers thin; controllers do not own DB or auth internals
globs: backend/src/**/*.js
alwaysApply: false
---

# Backend layers

| Layer | Owns | Must not own |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `controllers/` | req/res, status codes, call a service | DB, JWT, business rules |
| `services/` | business logic | Express req/res |
| `models/` | data shape / persistence | HTTP |
| `routes/` | wire path → controller | logic |
| `middleware/` | shared request concerns | feature business rules |
| `validators/` | input checks | side effects |

When asked for one layer, write only that layer. Wire-up is a separate request.
